The type definitions, request and response models, endpoint paths, retry
policy, and streaming reconnection semantics in this crate were ported from
that project, and the generated enums are still produced from its source.

Behavioral parity with alpaca-py was the original goal and is no longer the
goal: this crate targets the Alpaca API, and diverges from alpaca-py where
alpaca-py is incomplete or out of date. Comments cite the Python source where
the derivation is the point, and cite Alpaca's own documentation otherwise.

The response payloads under fixtures/go/ are derived from alpaca-trade-api-go
(https://github.com/alpacahq/alpaca-trade-api-go), Copyright 2021 Alpaca,
licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. They are used as test data.

